      tokenUtility: "Bitcoin\'s utility lies primarily as a store of value and a medium of exchange. Tokenized deposits and securities, as explored by the ECB, aim to provide utility for more efficient interbank settlements, faster trading, and reduced operational costs for traditional financial assets.",
      tokenomics: "For Bitcoin, tokenomics are characterized by a fixed supply cap of 21 million BTC, with new coins introduced through mining and halving events. For the broader market, the concept of tokenomics applies to various digital assets with diverse supply schedules, distribution models, and inflation/deflation mechanisms. Tokenized traditional assets would mirror the supply of their underlying real-world counterparts.",
