      bearCase: "The recurring theme of crypto-related fraud and money laundering, exemplified by the Israeli probe, will likely reinforce regulatory caution in India. This could lead to stricter controls, potential restrictions on certain types of crypto activities, or even a more prolonged period of regulatory uncertainty, hindering market growth and investor confidence.",
      neutralCase: "The Indian government will likely continue its cautious approach, focusing on developing a balanced regulatory framework that aims to mitigate risks without stifling innovation entirely. This \'wait and watch\' strategy, while slow, could eventually lead to a more stable and secure environment for digital assets, albeit with a slower pace of adoption than some market participants might desire.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "A \'Cautiously Regulated Growth\' scenario appears most probable for India. There\'s a high likelihood (60%) of increased regulatory scrutiny and a push for clearer laws, driven by global events and domestic concerns. This will likely lead to a period of consolidation among compliant players (30% probability) and enhanced investor protection measures (25%). However, the informal market will persist, posing ongoing challenges (15%).",
